{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Information, Data, and System Concepts "}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear every time you talk about data, information and system concepts."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.   "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Demonstratives as Pronouns and Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <b>demonstratives</b> to indicate the position of something or to give a characteristic to a noun. Although demonstrative pronouns and adjectives are similar, they have different uses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can find singular and plural demonstratives. We use different demonstratives to indicate how far an object is from the speaker. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"NEAR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"FAR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Singular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> This\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Plural\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> These\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Those\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br><i>  I do not understand the information in <b>this</b> file </i>(the file is near the speaker) </br><i> I see <b>that</b> application does not have the right codes. (the data is far from the speaker)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use two types of demonstratives for different purposes, so do not get confused. Let's look at each of them:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Demonstrative adjectives</b> go before the noun and indicate how far the object is from the speaker."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br><i><b>This information</b> is so valuable for the company. </br><b>That research report</b> demonstrates the importance of systems.</br><b> These applications</b> are a product of software engineering. </br><b>Those connections </b>mean the data is organized. </i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand,<b> demonstrative pronouns</b> replace a noun that we already talked about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  </br><i>I sent you some files last night. Analyze only <b>those</b> before the meeting. </br>You talked about different features, but <b>these</b> are not clear for me, there it too much data.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are some basic concepts that we need to understand when talking about computers. These are information, data and systems. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can understand this term as a group of facts that are not organized."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Then, we have information. This refers to processed data."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we think of a system, we have to consider two things: the elements that compose it and their functions. This means that those elements or components have different functions or tasks inside the system and they work together to keep this system going.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can talk more about that tutorial whenever you want."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Information, Data and System Concepts "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Systems concepts help us understand how systems work and how they interact. By making a clear distinction between information, data, and systems, you'll be able to interpret systems theory better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Although there's a significant distinction between these three concepts, we often use them when we talk about systems, software engineering, and information systems."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"COMPUTING AND SYSTEMS THEORY CONCEPTS\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><Information</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you enter and store information in a computer, it is data. However, if you print it or process it, it becomes information.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Data</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You enter it into a computer for processing, then you convert it into information with an \u2018easy to process' formula.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>System</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A group of components that work for specific objectives. For example, software and hardware integrate a computer system and work together to complete a function.  \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "run a program "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to execute a program, to get a program going or working"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Once we have this information organized and processed, we can use it to make decisions or to run programs. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "source"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "where something comes from, its origin"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can use data as a source of facts that the computer processes and shapes and then, we receive this as information.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "formula"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of numbers, words, or codes that indicates a process for an outcome"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When we receive data, we enter it for the computer to process it and with simple formulas, the computer can transform data into information. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "binary "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "consisting of two parts or has a combination with multiples of two"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can understand this term as a group of facts that are not organized. These sometimes come in binary code, or series of 0s and 1s. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "random "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "occurring for no particular reason or without a particular pattern, accidentally"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These sometimes come in binary code, or series of 0s and 1s; and can seem useless or random as they do not have a context. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "keep something going "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something to continue working"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This means that those elements or components have different functions or tasks inside the system and they work together to keep this system going.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about information, data and systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a descriptive chart about these concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write how these concepts work together and their importance."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your descriptive chart with the class and write more  characteristics."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about information, data and systems  concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make organize information, data and systems concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify information, data and systems concepts importance."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le01ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<b>Alan</b>: Good Morning Susan, the tutorial we have for this week is about the key elements for understanding computers, right?</br>\n<b>Susan</b>: Yes. There are some basic concepts that we need to understand when talking about computers. These are information, data and systems. Let's begin by talking about data!</br>\n<b>Alan</b>: Yes. We can understand this term as a group of facts that are not organized. These sometimes come in binary code, or series of 0s and 1s; and can seem useless or random as they do not have a context. We need to process and classify these facts before we can understand or use them."}, {"time": "41000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<b>Susan</b>: Then, we have information. This refers to processed data. </br>\n<b>Alan</b>: Exactly. When we receive data, we enter it for the computer to process it and with simple formulas, the computer can transform data into information. </br>\n<b>Susan</b>: So basically, we can use data as a source of facts that the computer processes and shapes and then, we receive this as information.  Once we have this information organized and processed, we can use it to make decisions or to run programs."}, {"time": "72000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<b>Alan</b>: Now, what about systems? </br>\n<b>Susan</b>: This one is a little bit more complex. A system is a group of components that you organize for a common purpose. When we think of a system, we have to consider two things: the elements that compose it and their functions. This means that those elements or components have different functions or tasks inside the system and they work together to keep this system going.  </br>\n<b>Alan</b>: I think it's all clear now, thank you so much for your help!</br>\n<b>Susan</b>: No problem! We can talk more about that tutorial whenever you want."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the concept